  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between ephedrine and DO4 through a multi-step mechanism involving SNU-387. Ephedrine is directly linked to SNU-387, which is a target of ephedrine and is itself a target of another compound, Dendocarbin K, and of the compound (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol, which ultimately targets DO4. This indicates that ephedrine may influence the biological activity of SNU-387, which in turn affects DO4 through a series of molecular interactions. The scores from the paths suggest a consistent and plausible pathway, though the exact nature of the interaction between ephedrine and SNU-387 remains unclear. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between ephedrine and DO4, but further investigation is needed to elucidate the precise molecular mechanisms involved.",
